#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# list_plot3d

#% text
# `list_plot3d(m)` draws the surface of a matrix of heights, the rows along y.

#% text
# `list_plot3d([[x1, y1, z1], ...])` draws a surface through scattered points.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Scattered points are interpolated on a grid (each grid point the inverse-distance-weighted mean of the points; far from all points there is no surface).

#% item
# The value is `image("path")`, a PNG with SVG and PDF copies next to it.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# Heights in a table:

#% cell
list_plot3d(table(sin(i/3)*cos(j/4), i, 20, j, 20))
#% output
#= image("list_plot3d.files/list_plot3d-1.png")

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Scattered points:

#% cell
seed(3); list_plot3d(map(p => [p[1], p[2], p[1]*p[2]], table([random_real(), random_real()], 40)))
#% output
#= image("list_plot3d.files/list_plot3d-2.png")

#% subsection
# Options

#% text
# Coloured by height:

#% cell
list_plot3d(table(i*j, i, 10, j, 10), color_function: viridis, mesh: none)
#% output
#= image("list_plot3d.files/list_plot3d-3.png")

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `plot3d`, `list_point_plot3d`, `list_density_plot`
